nap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:123:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:124:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:125:- 背景色为 Black。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:126:- 网格中散布着若干个大小相同的正方形彩色方块（如 3×3），每个方块为单一非背景色，方块之间不相邻。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:127:- 每两个相邻（水平或垂直方向上最近的一对）方块之间恰好有一个单像素的 Grey 箭头标记。箭头标记的具体形状为：箭头是由 3 个 Grey 像素组成的 L 形——一个像素在中心，另外两个像素分别在中心的同一侧相邻位置，形成指向某个方向的视觉箭头（例如指向右的箭头：中心像素 + 上方像素 + 下方像素构成\">\"形）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:128:- 箭头始终指向两个方块中的一个，表示颜色传递方向：从箭头背离的方块传向箭头指向的方块。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:129:- 所有方块和箭头形成一条或多条不分叉的链。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:130:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:131:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:132:- 沿每条链的箭头方向追踪传递路径。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:133:- 链中每个方块的颜色被替换为其上游方块（箭头来源方向）的颜色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:134:- 链首方块（没有上游的方块）变为背景色 Black。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:135:- 箭头标记在输出中被清除为背景色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:136:- 链尾方块获得其上游方块的原始颜色（即传递前的颜色，非传递后的）。所有传递同时发生，使用各方块的原始颜色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:137:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:138:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:139:解题者需要先从箭头的朝向识别传递方向，再追踪完整的传递链，最后理解颜色是\"同时传递\"而非逐步覆盖——\"箭头方向解码→链路追踪→同步颜色移位\"形成三层推理，其中同步传递的语义容易与逐步传递混淆。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:140:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:141:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:142:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:143:网格包含若干\"画笔\"对象和一个\"画布\"区域；每把画笔的颜色和朝向决定它在画布上绘制的笔画位置与方向，笔画长度则由画笔自身的像素数决定。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:144:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:145:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:146:- 背景色为 Black。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:147:- 网格右下角有一个矩形\"画布\"区域，边框为 Grey，内部为背景色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:148:- 画布外部散布着若干\"画笔\"对象，每个画笔是一个单色的 4-连通线段（水平或垂直的一排像素，长度 2-6 不等），颜色各不相同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:149:- 每个画笔的一端有一个相邻的单像素 Yellow 标记，位于画笔的某一侧（上/下/左/右），表示该画笔的\"笔尖方向\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:150:- 画布的一条边（上边或左边）上按等间距排列着与画笔同色的单像素\"锚点\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:151:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:152:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:153:- 将每个画笔与画布边上同色的锚点配对。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:154:- 从锚点出发，沿画笔的笔尖方向（由 Yellow 标记相对于画笔的方位决定）在画布内部绘制一条直线笔画。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:155:- 笔画的长度等于该画笔的像素数（不含 Yellow 标记）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:156:- 笔画颜色与画笔颜色相同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:157:- 画笔和 Yellow 标记在输出中保持不变；画布内未被笔画覆盖的区域保持为背景色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:158:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:159:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:160:解题者需要同时解码三种信息——颜色配对（画笔↔锚点）、方向（Yellow 标记的相对位置）、长度（画笔像素数）——并将它们组合才能确定画布上每条笔画的完整参数。单独看任何一条规则都很简单，但三者的交叉组合构成了需要多样例才能归纳的推理挑战。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/des.md:161:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:1:你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:2:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:3:每个参考题描述包含：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:4:- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:5:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:6:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:7:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:8:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:9:参考题目如下：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:10:<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"2ccd9fef\" lines=\"173-187\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:11:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:12:Predict the next panel in a framed sequence by continuing each scheduled colored interval.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:13:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:14:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:15:- The grid is made from three or more equal panels in one row or one column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:16:- The final input panel is the static target template; every earlier panel differs from it only by dynamic colors absent from the template.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:17:- Each dynamic color appears in a regular temporal schedule across the earlier panels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:18:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:19:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:20:- Keep the final template panel as the output canvas.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:21:- For every dynamic color whose schedule reaches the next panel, compare its last two appearances.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:22:- Extrapolate each one-dimensional interval along the color's changing row or column axis and paint that predicted mask.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:23:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:24:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:25:- The task is not asking for the last visible panel, but for the next frame after the blank/template slot.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:26:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:27:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:28:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:29:<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"342ae2ed\" lines=\"34-49\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:30:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:31:Draw the missing diagonal connector segment between each pair of same-color rectangular objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:32:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:33:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:34:- The grid has one dominant background color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:35:- Every foreground color appears as exactly two separated solid rectangular 4-connected objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:36:- The two rectangles of each color are diagonally offset with facing corners on a 45-degree line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:37:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:38:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:39:- Keep all existing rectangles unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:40:- For each foreground color, connect the lower facing corner of the upper rectangle to the upper facing corner of the lower rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:41:- Paint only the intervening background pixels on that diagonal, excluding the two endpoint pixels already in the rectangles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:42:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:43:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:44:- Same-color rectangles define the endpoints; the output completes the open diagonal between their nearest facing corners.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:45:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:46:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:47:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:48:<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"c4d1a9ae\" lines=\"28-48\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:49:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:50:Fill each vertical foreground band's background cells with the color of the next band to its right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:51:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:52:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:53:- The dominant color is the background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:54:- Each other color occupies a separate vertical band defined by that color's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:55:  minimum and maximum columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:56:- Within a band, all cells are either that band's color or background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:57:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:58:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:59:- Order the bands from left to right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:60:- In each band, replace background pixels with the color of the next band in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:61:  that order, wrapping from the rightmost band back to the leftmost.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:62:- Preserve all existing foreground pixels and all background pixels outside\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:63:  the bands.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:64:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:65:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:66:- The column bands form a cyclic palette legend: a band's gaps are completed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:67:  by borrowing the color from its right-hand neighbor, not by changing the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:68:  band's existing pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:69:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:70:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:71:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:72:<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5e6bbc0b\" lines=\"42-56\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:73:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:74:Compact the checkerboard's moving color toward the edge marked by the teal pixel, leaving a maroon swept trail on the marker line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:75:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:76:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:77:- A blue/black checkerboard with exactly one teal marker replacing a blue pixel on a non-corner edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:78:- The marker's checkerboard parity identifies the moving color (blue); the opposite parity is background (black).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:79:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:80:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:81:- If the marker is on the left or right edge, compact moving-color pixels in every row toward that side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:82:- If the marker is on the top or bottom edge, compact moving-color pixels in every column toward that side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:83:- Preserve the teal marker at its edge cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:84:- On the marker's row or column, color cells swept by shifted moving pixels maroon unless the final compacted line occupies them.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:85:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:86:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:87:The marker selects both the compression direction and the checkerboard color class that moves; maroon records the movement trail only along that marked line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:88:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:89:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:90:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:91:<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"a416fc5b\" lines=\"95-106\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:92:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:93:Add the two missing colored arms of a centered diamond-sprite motif, or clear a completed motif to a blank square.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:94:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:95:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:96:An 11x11 board has orange background and pink separator bars forming nine 3x3 cells. Occupied cells contain a four-pixel diamond sprite; the center cell and one neighboring cell are red, and a completed board may also contain one grey and one teal sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:97:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:98:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:99:With only the two red sprites present, preserve the board and add grey and teal diamond sprites 135 degrees clockwise and counterclockwise from the non-center red arm. If those expected grey and teal sprites are already present, output an all-background square whose side length is the total number of sprite pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:100:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:101:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:102:The non-center red sprite is an eight-neighbor direction from the center; the other two colored arms are fixed rotations of that direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:103:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:104:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:105:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:106:<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"b745798f\" lines=\"18-33\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:107:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:108:Expand each 3-pixel L marker into a same-color corner L on an empty background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:109:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:110:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:111:- The grid is an odd square with one dominant background color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:112:- Every foreground object is a monochromatic 4-connected 3-pixel L inside a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:113:  2x2 box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:114:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:115:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:116:- Clear the grid to the background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:117:- For each marker, map its L orientation to the corresponding outer corner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:118:  and draw that corner L in the marker color with arm length half the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:119:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:120:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:121:- The small marker is a miniature corner; its orientation, not its position,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:122:  chooses which outer corner receives the expanded L.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:123:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:124:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:125:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:126:<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"edcc2ff0\" lines=\"47-63\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:127:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:128:Keep only the lower-panel colors named by the top markers and expand each marker into an object-count bar.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:129:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:130:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:131:A black instruction strip sits above a non-black rectangular scene panel.  The strip contains one-cell markers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:132:in the first column, and each marker color is a candidate object color in the lower panel.  The lower panel has\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:133:a unique dominant background color and scattered 4-connected foreground objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:134:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:135:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:136:In the lower panel, preserve objects whose colors appear as top markers and recolor every other foreground\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:137:object to the panel background.  In the instruction strip, replace each marker by a horizontal run from column 0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:138:whose length is the number of 4-connected lower-panel objects of that marker color; erase markers with count 0.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:139:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:140:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:141:The top strip is a color filter plus a compact count summary: marker colors select which lower-panel objects\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:142:survive, and their bars report the number of surviving objects by color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:143:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:144:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:145:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:146:<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"ac0c2ac3\" lines=\"7-19\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:147:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:148:Fill each centered square ring with the color of the marker at that ring distance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:149:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:150:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:151:The input is an odd square grid with a dominant background color and one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:152:non-background marker for every Chebyshev distance from the grid center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:153:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:154:The output replaces the background with concentric square rings centered on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:155:the middle cell; every cell at distance d from the center takes the color of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:156:the unique marker whose distance from the center is d.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:157:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:158:The scattered markers are not objects to move; their Chebyshev distances\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:159:form a palette for the centered square rings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:160:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:161:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:162:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:163:<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"825aa9e9\" lines=\"111-125\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:164:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:165:Drop the moving-color objects downward until they rest above a one-row cushion before the obstacle or bottom edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:166:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:167:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:168:- The grid has exactly three colors: empty background, a stationary obstacle/floor color, and a moving object color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:169:- The obstacle color is the unique non-background role that touches the bottom edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:170:- Moving pixels start outside the obstacle cells, outside the row directly above each obstacle pixel, and outside the bottom row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:171:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:172:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:173:- Keep the background and obstacle pixels fixed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:174:- Treat obstacle pixels, cells directly above obstacle pixels, and the bottom row as blocked.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:175:- Repeatedly move every 4-connected moving-color object one row down when its translated shape does not hit blocked cells or another moving object.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:176:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:177:Key insight: The visible floor has an invisible one-row cushion above it, so the objects fall under gravity but stop with one empty row before the floor or the grid bottom.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:178:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:179:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:180:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:181:<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"71e489b6\" lines=\"7-19\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:182:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:183:Highlight black defects in blue foreground by surrounding them with orange.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:184:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:185:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:186:- Blue (1) foreground on black (0) bg; small black holes or protrusions within blue regions; occasional thin blue spurs into black areas.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:187:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:188:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:189:- Thin blue pixels mostly surrounded by black are absorbed into the background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:190:- Small black components (≤3 cells) and leaf pixels of larger black components are \"defects.\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:191:- Each defect gets an orange (7) 8-neighbor halo; the defect pixels themselves stay black.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:192:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:193:Key insight: Only structural anomalies—tiny isolated patches and dangling endpoints—are marked, not bulk black regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:194:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:195:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:196:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:197:<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d753a70b\" lines=\"81-93\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:198:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:199:Red diamond outlines contract by one layer and gray diamond outlines expand by one layer while other objects stay fixed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:200:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:201:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:202:- A 16x16 orange-background grid contains one-cell-thick Manhattan-diamond outlines.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:203:- Red and gray outlines are the changing objects; other colored diamond outlines are static.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:204:- Some outlines may be clipped by the grid boundary, but their visible pixels still fit a clipped Manhattan-distance contour.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:205:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:206:- Clear all red and gray pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:207:- Red objects are redrawn with the same diamond center and radius minus one.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:208:- Gray objects are redrawn with radius plus one; an ambiguous edge-clipped growing arc continues away from the nearest perpendicular edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:209:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:210:- The task is not about moving whole objects: each changing object is a contour of a diamond, and the visible operation is one step of contour contraction or expansion.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:211:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:212:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:213:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:214:<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"b9e38dc0\" lines=\"7-18\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:215:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:216:Fill the region enclosed by a wall sprite and radiate color outward through its opening.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:217:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:218:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:219:- bg = most common color. Wall = most frequent non-bg color, forming a partial enclosure (e.g. U-shape).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:220:- A fill-color pixel sits inside the enclosed area. Other non-bg pixels may act as obstacles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:221:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:222:- Flood-fill the enclosed area with the fill color, radiating outward through the wall's open end.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:223:- Obstacles cast \"shadows\" along the radiate direction, blocking fill behind them.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:224:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:225:Key insight: The wall endpoints define the opening direction; fill radiates outward through it, and obstacles block propagation along that same axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:226:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:227:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:228:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:229:<reference_puzzle index=\"13\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"5961cc34\" lines=\"8-21\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:230:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:231:Build a red ray network by activating blue blobs via directional green ports.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:232:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:233:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:234:- bg = most common color. Large blue blobs with adjacent green pixels marking port directions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:235:- Start marker: yellow pixel atop a short red segment at grid bottom.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:236:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:237:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:238:- Extend a ray upward from start; on hitting a blue blob, recolor it red.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:239:- Activated blobs emit thick rays through green ports until boundary or another blob.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:240:- Cascade until no new blobs are reached.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:241:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:242:Key insight: Green pixels encode ray direction and width; the network activates as a chain reaction from one start point.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:243:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:244:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:245:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:246:<reference_puzzle index=\"14\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"14b8e18c\" lines=\"40-57\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:247:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:248:Mark every complete square object with red pixels just outside its corners.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:249:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:250:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:251:- A uniform background contains one or more monochrome 4-connected foreground objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:252:- The relevant objects are square frames or filled squares: their bbox is square\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:253:  and all cells on the bbox border have the object's color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:254:- Non-square bars and incomplete fragments may also appear and are ignored.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:255:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:256:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:257:- Keep the input unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:258:- For each complete square object, paint red on the two outside background\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:259:  pixels orthogonally adjacent to each of the square's four corners.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:260:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:261:Key insight: The transformation is not based on size or color; it selects\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:262:objects whose bounding box is a complete square border and labels only their\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:263:exposed outer corner-adjacent cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:264:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:265:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:266:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:267:<reference_puzzle index=\"15\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"d8e07eb2\" lines=\"29-47\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:268:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:269:Look up query glyphs in a reference table and mark whether they form a line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:270:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:271:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:272:- Teal background with two full-width pink separator rows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:273:- Above the first separator is a query row of 5x5 glyph cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:274:- Between separators is a reference table of the same 5x5 cells; a glyph is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:275:  identified by both its color and its 3x3 shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:276:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:277:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:278:- Green-fill the background inside every table cell whose glyph exactly\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:279:  appears in the query row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:280:- If the matched table cells form one complete row or one complete column,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:281:  also green-fill the query band and the bottom verdict band.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:282:- Otherwise leave the query band unchanged and fill the bottom verdict band red.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:283:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:284:Key insight: The bottom color is not a count; it is the yes/no answer to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:285:whether the queried glyphs align as a full row or column in the table.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:286:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:287:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:288:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:289:<reference_puzzle index=\"16\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"db615bd4\" lines=\"111-130\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:290:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:291:Thicken the sparse frame and stamp the external sparse sprites into it in positional order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:292:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:293:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:294:The grid has a dominant background color, a regular lattice color, one large\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:295:sparse rectangular frame, and one or more external monochrome sprites whose\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:296:pixels also sit on a two-step lattice.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:297:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:298:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:299:Use the largest sparse rectangular perimeter as the frame. Clear that frame\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:300:region and the external sprite pixels to background, draw a solid one-pixel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:301:border in the frame color, solidify each sparse sprite into its contiguous\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:302:two-step mask, and place the sprites inside the frame with equal gaps.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:303:Wide frames receive sprites left-to-right by source position; tall frames\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:304:receive them top-to-bottom by source position.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:305:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:306:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:307:The frame supplies ordered slots: the sprite-to-slot assignment is by visible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:308:source order, not by numeric color or by matching individual cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:309:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:310:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:311:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:312:<reference_puzzle index=\"17\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"a395ee82\" lines=\"9-24\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:313:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:314:Stamp translated copies of a monochrome template guided by a singleton pixel layout.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:315:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:316:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:317:- bg = background. A large monochrome shape (template, color T).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:318:- Singleton pixels elsewhere: exactly one is color T (layout origin); the rest share color O (overlap color).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:319:- Singletons sit on a uniform-spacing lattice.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:320:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:321:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:322:- Convert each singleton's offset from the origin into coarse lattice units.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:323:- Place a template copy at each offset, scaled by template height/width.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:324:- The origin's copy is painted O instead of T.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:325:- Any pixel covered by two or more copies is also recolored to O.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:326:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:327:Key insight: The single T-colored singleton identifies both the origin position and the \"self\" copy, which is uniquely recolored.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:328:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:329:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:330:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:331:<reference_puzzle index=\"18\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"4a21e3da\" lines=\"8-20\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:332:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:333:Cut a sprite along border-control rays and slide pieces to grid corners.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:334:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:335:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:336:- bg, fg (main object, ~centered), ctrl (1-2 pixels on grid edges).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:337:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:338:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:339:- Draw rays inward from each ctrl pixel along its row/col, painting only bg cells up to the farthest fg pixel (intermittent).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:340:- Rays partition the grid; fg on the cut line stays in place.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:341:- Cut pieces in regions touching a control edge slide to that corner; others vanish.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:342:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:343:Key insight: Only regions sharing a border edge with a control pixel keep their piece; the ray skips fg cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:344:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:345:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:346:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:347:<reference_puzzle index=\"19\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"652646ff\" lines=\"84-105\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:348:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:349:Recover each partially hidden 6x6 ring sprite and stack complete copies from top layer to bottom layer.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:350:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:351:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:352:- The dominant color is the background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:353:- Several non-background colors are visible fragments of the same 12-pixel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:354:  outline ring in a 6x6 box; small off-template marker pixels are noise.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:355:- Ring fragments overlap, so upper rings replace some expected pixels of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:356:  lower rings, and a ring may also be clipped by the input boundary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:357:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:358:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:359:- Identify every substantial color whose pixels all lie on one translated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:360:  copy of the ring template.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:361:- For each missing in-bounds template pixel, the color currently occupying\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:362:  that pixel is above the hidden ring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:363:- Topologically sort these occlusion relations from top to bottom, then draw\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:364:  one complete 6x6 ring for each color in that order on a background canvas.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:365:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:366:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:367:- The output is not a crop of the scene; it is the layer stack of complete\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:368:  ring sprites reconstructed from their visible fragments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:369:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:370:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:371:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:372:<reference_puzzle index=\"20\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"a25697e4\" lines=\"9-23\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:373:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:374:Dock movable tools into border-anchored frames by filling cavities.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:375:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:376:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:377:- bg = most common color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:378:- Border-touching components cluster into anchor frames with interior bg cavities.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:379:- Non-border 2-color components are movable tools.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:380:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:381:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:382:- Match each tool to a frame whose cavity size equals one of its color-region counts.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:383:- Rotate/flip the tool so one color fills the cavity exactly; the other stays outside.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:384:- If the docking orientation uses a reflection, swap the tool's two colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:385:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:386:Key insight: Cavity size determines tool–frame pairing; reflection triggers color swap.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:387:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:388:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:389:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:390:你的任务：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:391:以参考题为标杆，运用发散性思维进行创新扩展。请发挥创造力，构思全新且巧妙的推理谜题。用中文创造全新的 ARC 谜题描述。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:392:创新方式包括但不限于：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:393:**机制重组**：将多道参考题各自的核心机制提取出来，组合成一个新的多步管道，用到新的场景。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:394:**机制变异**：取几道参考题的核心机制，以机制为基础进行创新并与其他多种机制进行创新重组，使解题路径发生质变而非量变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:395:**逆向构造**：取一道参考题的输出模式，思考\"什么样的输入规则能产生类似的输出结构但需要完全不同的推理过程\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:396:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:397:严格使用下面的 XML 风格格式输出：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:398:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:399:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:400:- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:401:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:402:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:403:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:404:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:405:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:406:请一次性生成5个`<new_puzzle>`，若有较多合适的创新，也可以生成更多，不设上限，但不要输出额外解释。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:407:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:408:注意事项：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:409:1. 任务不应依赖大量先验知识或复杂计算，而应依赖对模式、结构与空间关系的直觉推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:410:2. 关于\"计算\"的边界：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:411:   - **允许使用**（这些都是人类能心算的视觉量）：数像素 / 孔洞 / 对象 / 邻居（≤10 量级）、比大小、按某个可见属性排序、奇偶判断、取最大 / 最小、用一个计数值作为另一个等量几何量（如 N 个像素 → 长度 N 的射线、面积 N → 边长 N）、判断接触 / 相邻 / 包含、粗略中心位置（簇的视觉中点）、\"距离\"作为\"几步\"而不是公式等人类能够直观感受计算的内容。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:412:   - **禁止使用**（这些是算法量而非视觉量，会迫使解题者依赖公式而非视觉直觉）：曼哈顿 / 欧氏 / Chebyshev 距离作为精确查表键、凸包面积、二进制位编码 / 位运算、模运算（取模） / 余数、拓扑距离（BFS / 最短路 / 跳数）、精确几何质心坐标、凸角 / 凹角计数等复杂且不易被看出来的计算都是禁止使用的。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:413:3. 问题必须能从少量示例中推断出来（通常为 3 对训练样例 + 1 个测试样例）。设计时从人类解题者的视觉角度思考：规则涉及的所有关键要素（对象、关系、属性）必须在网格上肉眼可见，不应依赖人眼无法直接观察到的隐含信息（例如颜色id和颜色亮度是禁止使用的）或需要推算的隐藏属性。规则背后的逻辑本身可以有一定挑战性，但解题所需的所有线索必须能从网格中直接获取。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:414:4. 生成的问题描述旨在促进后续用于创建题目网格的代码生成。因此，对输入 / 输出网格的描述以及规则总结必须极其详细；语言风格应易于理解；对于特定对象（如箭头），必须在描述中明确其绘制方式。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:415:5. 描述谜题时避免使用 0 或 1 这类颜色编号；应使用颜色名称，例如 \"red\"。可用颜色如下：Black、Blue、Red、Green、Yellow、Grey、Magenta、Orange、Azure、Maroon。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:416:6. 新题的核心推理机制应明显不同——即从观察样例到归纳规则的认知路径不同，而不仅仅是场景、对象或颜色不同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:417:7. 题目难度应来自机制的隐蔽性而非步骤数。用参考题作为难度标尺——如果你生成的题一个样例就能猜到规则，说明机制太透明，需要加深隐蔽性。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:418:8. 优先从参考题的机制出发进行重组或推演，而非从物理隐喻出发。物理隐喻容易导致大量题目归结为一种模式，例如\"沿方向移动到阻挡处停止\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:419:9. 题目的难度优先来自规则的**结构层数**，而不是单一步骤的复杂度。关于\"结构层数\"的判定标准：**只有解题者需要主动推理才能完成的步骤才算一层**。肉眼一扫即可获得的信息（如\"找到缺口在哪一侧\"、\"数出像素个数\"、\"识别哪个对象最大\"）不构成独立的推理层——它们只是变换的前置输入，不增加认知难度。真正的多层结构是指每一层都需要解题者发现一个非显然的规律。以两层结构为例：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:420:   - ✗ 伪两层：\"找到缺口方向\"→\"把东西推到对面\" — 第一步肉眼可见，实际只有一层推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:421:   - ✓ 真两层：\"通过孔洞数量匹配颜色图例\"→\"用匹配到的颜色重绘对象\" — 两步都需要非平凡的归纳。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:422:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:423:   如果你发现自己写出的题只是\"对每个对象，根据它的某个属性做某变换\"的单步规则，请引入一个需要主动推理的前置步骤。**用堆叠 tie-break 规则或复杂数学公式来\"加难度\"是劣解；用多一层需要归纳的结构嵌套来\"加难度\"才是好解**。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:424:10. 在符合ARC题目和提示词要求的基础上，鼓励尝试创新规则为多层结构的题目，不局限于两层，可以创新三层或四层结构的题目，但不可为了多结构层数违背要求。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:425:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:426:生成后对生成的题执行以下四项审查（审查内容不需要保存到文件）：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:427:1. 原创性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:428:  新题不可与上述参考题相同或类似，不可只是替换颜色、方向、对象类型等表层要素。判断标准：新题的核心推理路径应与任何一道参考题不同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:429:2. 确定性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:430:  规则完全确定，同一输入只能产生唯一输出，每一步操作都有明确定义。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:431:3. 可实现性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:432:  所有必要细节都已给出——对象如何生成、如何识别、如何变换、边界情况如何处理，读完描述后可以直接写代码。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:433:4. ARC 合规性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:434:  网格尺寸合理（≤30×30），使用颜色不超过 10 种，规则复杂度适中，人类能从 3-5 个样例中发现规律。没有使用上述注意事项第二条禁止使用的复杂计算。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/5/prompt.md:435:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
